#: ../../guide/filter.rst:3
msgid "Filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:5
msgid "Filters decide whether an update should reach a handler. Every observer call — ``@dp.new_message(...)``, ``@router.inline_message(...)`` — accepts an arbitrary number of filters as positional arguments. All filters must pass for the handler to be triggered, and the observer stops propagation at the **first** matching handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:18
msgid "Built-in filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:20
msgid "All of these live in :mod:`aiorubi.filters` (re-exported from ``aiorubi.filters.command``, ``...state``, etc.): ``Command``, ``CommandStart``, ``CommandObject``, ``StateFilter``, ``MagicData``, ``ExceptionTypeFilter``, ``ExceptionMessageFilter``, the combinators ``and_f`` / ``or_f`` / ``invert_f``, and the base class ``Filter`` (alias ``BaseFilter``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:28
msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:30
msgid "`aiorubi.filters.command.Command(*values, commands=None, prefix=\"/\", ignore_case=False, ignore_mention=False, magic=None)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:32
msgid "Matches text messages that start with one of the given commands. Works only with :class:`~aiorubi.types.message.Message` events that have a ``text``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:35
msgid "``values`` / ``commands`` — command names (``\"start\"``) or compiled regular expressions; ``BotCommand`` objects are accepted too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:37
msgid "``prefix`` — allowed prefix characters, default ``\"/\"``. Pass ``\"/!\"`` to accept both ``/start`` and ``!start``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:39
msgid "``ignore_case`` — case-fold matching (does not apply to regexp patterns)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:40
msgid "``ignore_mention`` — by default a command addressed to another bot (``/start@other_bot``) does not match; set ``True`` to ignore the mention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:43
msgid "``magic`` — an extra :class:`~aiorubi.utils.magic_filter.MagicFilter` applied to the parsed :class:`~aiorubi.filters.command.CommandObject`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:46
msgid "When the filter passes it injects the ``command`` keyword argument — a frozen dataclass with ``prefix``, ``command``, ``mention``, ``args``, ``regexp_match`` and the helpers ``.mentioned`` and ``.text``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:56
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.filters.command.CommandStart` is a shortcut for ``Command(\"start\")`` with deep-link validation: ``CommandStart(deep_link=True, deep_link_encoded=True)`` requires a payload argument and base64-decodes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:62
msgid "StateFilter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:64
msgid "`aiorubi.filters.state.StateFilter(*states)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:66
msgid "Checks the update against the current FSM state (see :doc:`fsm`). Accepts any mix of :class:`~aiorubi.fsm.state.State` objects, ``StatesGroup`` classes/instances, raw strings, ``None`` and the ``\"*\"`` wildcard — at least one is required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:79
msgid "Subclassing a ``StatesGroup`` includes the parent's states in the check. Passing a :class:`~aiorubi.fsm.state.State` as decorator filter is equivalent to the plain ``Form.name`` shorthand shown in :doc:`fsm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:84
msgid "CallbackData (ButtonId)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:86
msgid "Rubika inline keypads carry a ``button_id`` string in the ``aux_data`` of an :class:`~aiorubi.types.inline_message.InlineMessage`. The :mod:`aiorubi.filters.callback_data` module provides a structured wrapper for it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:91
msgid "``aiorubi.filters.callback_data.ButtonId``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:93
msgid "A pydantic model base class. Subclass it with a required ``prefix=`` keyword and declare the payload fields; then use ``.pack()`` when building keypads and ``.filter()`` as the handler filter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:117
msgid "``Nav.filter(rule=None)`` returns an :class:`~aiorubi.filters.callback_data.InlineMessageFilter` which unpacks the incoming ``button_id`` and injects it as the ``button_id`` argument. Encodable field types: ``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``, ``Enum``, ``UUID``, ``Decimal``, ``Fraction`` and ``None`` (optional fields). The packed id must stay under 64 bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:125
msgid "MagicData"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:127
msgid "`aiorubi.filters.magic_data.MagicData(magic_data: MagicFilter)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:129
msgid "Resolves a magic-filter expression against the whole handler *context* — the event (as ``F.event``) plus every keyword the dispatcher provides (``bot``, ``state``, ``raw_state``, ``event_chat``, ``event_from_user``, …):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:142
msgid "ExceptionTypeFilter / ExceptionMessageFilter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:144
msgid "For the ``error`` observer, whose event is an :class:`~aiorubi.types.error_event.ErrorEvent`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:157
msgid "``ExceptionMessageFilter`` injects the regexp match as ``match_exception``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:161
msgid "MagicFilter — the ``F`` object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:163
msgid "``F`` (exported from :mod:`aiorubi`) is a :class:`aiorubi.utils.magic_filter.MagicFilter` instance. Indexing or calling attributes on it *builds* a filter expression; the expression is resolved against the event when a filter check runs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:180
msgid "The result of any expression is a valid filter, so you can mix ``F`` with the built-ins freely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:184
msgid "Storing results with ``as_()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:186
msgid "aiorubi extends the upstream magic-filter with ``as_(name)``: when the filter passes, the resolved value is injected into the handler under ``name``:"
msgstr ""

