msgid "Writing custom filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:200
msgid "Async and sync function filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:202
msgid "The simplest filter is a function. It receives the event plus the same contextual keyword arguments as a handler and returns ``bool`` — or a ``dict`` whose entries are injected into the handler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:213
msgid "Synchronous functions work too — they are executed in a thread via :func:`asyncio.to_thread`, so long CPU-bound checks do not block the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:217
msgid "Class-based filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:219
msgid "Subclass :class:`~aiorubi.filters.base.Filter` and override the async ``__call__``. Constructor arguments make the filter configurable and instances are reusable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:243
msgid "Returning ``False`` skips the handler; returning ``True`` passes; returning a ``dict`` passes **and** merges the entries into the handler kwargs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:246
msgid "Lambdas and ``F`` both work as drop-in callables — the dispatcher detects ``MagicFilter`` instances (including the plain ``magic_filter`` package object) automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:251
msgid "Combining filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:253
msgid "**Positional arguments** on an observer are combined with logical AND: all must pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:255
msgid "``&`` / ``|`` / ``~`` on magic-filter expressions build combined expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:257
msgid "``and_f``, ``or_f`` and ``invert_f`` combine arbitrary filters (class-based or functions):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:267
msgid "``~filter`` (invert) works on any :class:`~aiorubi.filters.base.Filter` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:271
msgid "Filter order and short-circuiting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:273
msgid "Two independent short-circuits are at play:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:275
msgid "**Within one handler** — filters are checked in declaration order and the check stops at the first failure. Put cheap filters first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/filter.rst:284
msgid "**Within one observer** — handlers are evaluated in registration order and propagation stops at the first fully matching handler. A handler can pass control to the next one by raising :class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.event.bases.SkipHandler`. Router-level filters (``observer.filter(...)``) are checked before handler filters."
msgstr ""

